{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787531003146,"sessionID":"ses_fceda74b8ffec0f01p0fDyvTkH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-81c1637340d4636f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-kZFwBF/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-workspace/prompt.md"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-kZFwBF/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-workspace/prompt.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Workspace worker: securitized-product trade capture\n2: \n3: Build the interactive application, state, blotter, review panel, and responsive\n4: visual system for the synthetic `/trade-capture` route. Read the product brief,\n5: frozen contract, domain types, and owned stubs first. Consume the finished\n6: domain and the separately owned ticket/insights interfaces; do not duplicate\n7: their work.\n8: \n9: You may change only:\n10: \n11: - `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`\n12: - `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`\n13: - `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`\n14: - `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts`\n15: - `app/trade-capture/state/selectors.ts`\n16: - `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`\n17: \n18: ## Reducer and selector behavior\n19: \n20: - Keep the frozen state shape and action names. `draft-changed` refreshes live\n21:   exceptions. `reset` restores a copied deterministic empty draft and clears\n22:   editing state and exceptions.\n23: - `save-draft`, `validate`, and `book` use the corresponding domain lifecycle\n24:   function with the supplied context, replace an edited record or append a new\n25:   one, select the result, then reset the edit/draft area. Booking errors may\n26:   propagate because the UI prevents the action while errors exist.\n27: - `edit` loads a non-cancelled record into a clean `TradeDraft`, preserves its\n28:   internal ID through `editingTradeId`, and refreshes exceptions. `cancel`\n29:   calls the domain helper, preserves the record and its selection, and cannot\n30:   delete history.\n31: - Search internal/client trade IDs, security ID, deal, and counterparty without\n32:   case sensitivity. Apply product and status filters together. Implement all\n33:   three sorts, descending, with internal trade ID as the deterministic final\n34:   tie-breaker. Selectors and reducer remain pure and import no React.\n35: - `selectDeskSummary` summarizes all records, not the filtered subset.\n36: \n37: ## Application behavior\n38: \n39: - Compose the existing `TradeTicket` and `DeskInsights` with your blotter and\n40:   review. The first render must keep the synthetic notice, totals, ticket,\n41:   validation status, blotter, and selected-record panel visible.\n42: - Dispatch IDs and ISO timestamps only when a user triggers a lifecycle action.\n43:   Use browser-native APIs; do not add dependencies. A small local synthetic ID\n44:   format is enough.\n45: - Validation summary uses `role=\"status\"` and explains error versus warning\n46:   counts. Do not calculate or validate in the component.\n47: \n48: ## Blotter and review behavior\n49: \n50: - Render all six product and four status filter choices, search, and all three\n51:   sorts. Use a semantic table with caption. Its horizontal scroll wrapper must\n52:   be focusable, `role=\"region\"`, and labelled. Row selection is a real button\n53:   with `aria-pressed`.\n54: - Show useful identity, side, execution, current face, price, principal, and\n55:   status columns with readable number/date formatting.\n56: - Review shows selected trade identity, status, economics, exceptions,\n57:   read-only allocations, notes, and complete audit history. Editing is allowed\n58:   only when not cancelled. Cancellation is enabled only when booked and has a\n59:   plain visible explanation otherwise.\n60: \n61: ## Visual system\n62: \n63: - Make the route feel like a focused institutional control surface, with a\n64:   strong hierarchy, compact readable data, visible status treatments, and\n65:   clear focus states. Keep it distinct from the benchmark dashboard.\n66: - Every CSS selector must begin with `.tc-`; no `:root`, universal selector,\n67:   bare element selector, global reset, or dashboard selector is allowed.\n68: - Keep the page usable at desktop and 390 pixels without page-level horizontal\n69:   overflow. The blotter may scroll only inside its labelled region. Include a\n70:   breakpoint no wider than 760 pixels and visible `:focus-visible` styling.\n71: - Do not add assets, dependencies, data persistence, network behavior, inline\n72:   styles, or real financial/client information.\n73: \n74: Run only `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`. In the final response, report\n75: changed files, check results, and any remaining limitation. Do not claim\n76: browser verification or production readiness.\n\n(End of file - total 76 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Workspace worker: securitized-product trade capture\n\nBuild the interactive application, state, blotter, review panel, and responsive\nvisual system for the synthetic `/trade-capture` route. Read the product brief,\nfrozen contract, domain types, and owned stubs first. Consume the finished\ndomain and the separately owned ticket/insights interfaces; do not duplicate\ntheir work.\n\nYou may change only:\n\n- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/state/selectors.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`\n\n## Reducer and selector behavior\n\n- Keep the frozen state shape and action names. `draft-changed` refreshes live","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-kZFwBF/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-workspace/prompt.md","text":"# Workspace worker: securitized-product trade capture\n\nBuild the interactive application, state, blotter, review panel, and responsive\nvisual system for the synthetic `/trade-capture` route. Read the product brief,\nfrozen contract, domain types, and owned stubs first. Consume the finished\ndomain and the separately owned ticket/insights interfaces; do not duplicate\ntheir work.\n\nYou may change only:\n\n- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/state/selectors.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`\n\n## Reducer and selector behavior\n\n- Keep the frozen state shape and action names. `draft-changed` refreshes live\n  exceptions. `reset` restores a copied deterministic empty draft and clears\n  editing state and exceptions.\n- `save-draft`, `validate`, and `book` use the corresponding domain lifecycle\n  function with the supplied context, replace an edited record or append a new\n  one, select the result, then reset the edit/draft area. Booking errors may\n  propagate because the UI prevents the action while errors exist.\n- `edit` loads a non-cancelled record into a clean `TradeDraft`, preserves its\n  internal ID through `editingTradeId`, and refreshes exceptions. `cancel`\n  calls the domain helper, preserves the record and its selection, and cannot\n  delete history.\n- Search internal/client trade IDs, security ID, deal, and counterparty without\n  case sensitivity. Apply product and status filters together. Implement all\n  three sorts, descending, with internal trade ID as the deterministic final\n  tie-breaker. Selectors and reducer remain pure and import no React.\n- `selectDeskSummary` summarizes all records, not the filtered subset.\n\n## Application behavior\n\n- Compose the existing `TradeTicket` and `DeskInsights` with your blotter and\n  review. The first render must keep the synthetic notice, totals, ticket,\n  validation status, blotter, and selected-record panel visible.\n- Dispatch IDs and ISO timestamps only when a user triggers a lifecycle action.\n  Use browser-native APIs; do not add dependencies. A small local synthetic ID\n  format is enough.\n- Validation summary uses `role=\"status\"` and explains error versus warning\n  counts. Do not calculate or validate in the component.\n\n## Blotter and review behavior\n\n- Render all six product and four status filter choices, search, and all three\n  sorts. Use a semantic table with caption. Its horizontal scroll wrapper must\n  be focusable, `role=\"region\"`, and labelled. Row selection is a real button\n  with `aria-pressed`.\n- Show useful identity, side, execution, current face, price, principal, and\n  status columns with readable number/date formatting.\n- Review shows selected trade identity, status, economics, exceptions,\n  read-only allocations, notes, and complete audit history. Editing is allowed\n  only when not cancelled. Cancellation is enabled only when booked and has a\n  plain visible explanation otherwise.\n\n## Visual system\n\n- Make the route feel like a focused institutional control surface, with a\n  strong hierarchy, compact readable data, visible status treatments, and\n  clear focus states. Keep it distinct from the benchmark dashboard.\n- Every CSS selector must begin with `.tc-`; no `:root`, universal selector,\n  bare element selector, global reset, or dashboard selector is allowed.\n- Keep the page usable at desktop and 390 pixels without page-level horizontal\n  overflow. The blotter may scroll only inside its labelled region. Include a\n  breakpoint no wider than 760 pixels and visible `:focus-visible` styling.\n- Do not add assets, dependencies, data persistence, network behavior, inline\n  styles, or real financial/client information.\n\nRun only `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`. In the final response, report\nchanged files, check results, and any remaining limitation. Do not claim\nbrowser verification or production readiness.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":76,"totalLines":76,"truncated":false}},"title":"benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-workspace/prompt.md","time":{"start":1787531003135,"end":1787531003142}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding of the domain. Let me also check the task prompt (T7-trade-workspace) and any rubric to see if there's more detail, and check the existing dashboard CSS to make my design \"distinct from the benchmark dashboard\". Let me read the task prompt for T7-trade-workspace.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0312684f8001hOxUGqh32HgdfQ","sessionID":"ses_fceda74b8ffec0f01p0fDyvTkH","messageID":"msg_03126703c001hroktw65TRcqnj"}}
