er-color: #93cbb8;\n\n  Line 491:   background: var(--green-soft);\n\n  Line 499:   border: 1px solid var(--ink);\n\n  Line 501:   background: var(--ink);\n\n  Line 502:   color: white;\n\n  Line 517:   color: #ffffff;\n\n  Line 518:   font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n\n  Line 528:   color: #bdc9c5;\n\n  Line 545:   background: var(--blue-soft);\n\n  Line 546:   color: var(--blue-dark);\n\n  Line 547:   font-family: var(--font-geist-mono), monospace;\n\n  Line 560:   border-top: 3px solid var(--orange);\n\n  Line 562:   background: var(--paper-deep);\n\n  Line 567:   border-color: var(--blue);\n\n  Line 571:   border-color: var(--green);\n\n  Line 584:   color: var(--muted);\n\n  Line 589:   border-left: 4px solid var(--blue) !important;\n\n  Line 602:   border: 1px solid var(--line);\n\n  Line 603:   border-radius: var(--radius);\n\n  Line 604:   background: var(--white);\n\n  Line 610:   background: var(--blue);\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":100,"truncated":true},"title":"background|color|font-family|--","time":{"start":1787531155801,"end":1787531155829}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I have enough context. Let me now write the implementation.\n\nLet me be careful about a few details:\n\n1. In the reducer — for `edit` action, when I load the trade into a draft. Also the frozen state shape and action names must stay the same.\n\n2. In selectors — sorting: I'll implement a general comparator.\n\nNote on stable sorting: JS `Array.prototype.sort` — since ES2019 it's stable, but with a tie-breaker comparison anyway it's deterministic.\n\nFor selectors:\n```ts\nfunction compareByIdDesc(a: Trade, b: Trade): number {\n  return b.internalTradeId.localeCompare(a.internalTradeId);\n}\n```\nHmm, lexicographic on IDs — deterministic. Fine.\n\nFor the sort comparator:\n```ts\nconst SORT COMPARATORS: Record<TradeSort, (a: Trade, b: Trade) => number> = {\n  \"execution-desc\": (a, b) => b.executionTimestamp.localeCompare(a.executionTimestamp),\n  \"current-face-desc\": (a, b) => b.economics.currentFace - a.economics.currentFace,\n  \"gross-principal-desc\": (a, b) => b.economics.grossPrincipal - a.economics.grossPrincipal,\n};\nfunction sortTrades(trades, sort) {\n  const comparator = COMPARATORS[sort];\n  return [...trades].sort((a, b) => comparator(a, b) || compareByIdDesc(a, b));\n}\n```\n\nSearch: lowercase contains across internalTradeId, clientTradeId, securityId, issuerDeal, counterparty.\n\n3. In app component — create context helper:\n```ts\nfunction createLifecycleContext(): LifecycleContext {\n  const stamp = Date.now().toString(36);\n  const random = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8).toUpperCase();\n  return { id: `SYNTH-TRADE-${stamp}-${random}`, at: new Date().toISOString() };\n}\n```\n\nWait — for `edit` and `cancel`, the context is only needed for audit. For `cancel`, the audit event id uses context.id — the audit function uses `${context.id}-${action}` for the audit event id, and trade identity comes from existing record. So generating a fresh ID for cancel context is fine — it's used for the audit event `id` and `at`. OK.\n\nValidation summary in the app:\n```tsx\nconst errorCount = ...\nconst warningCount = ...\n<p className=\"tc-validation\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n  {errorCount} validation error{errorCount === 1 ? \"\" : \"s\"}, {warningCount} warning{...} in the current ticket draft.\n</p>\n```\nHmm — the test asserts html matches `/role=\"status\"/` on the /trade-capture route — the validation paragraph must render on first render. Good.\n\nWait, also \"The first render must keep the synthetic notice, totals, ticket, validation status, blotter, and selected-record panel visible.\" The stub satisfies all of these. Keep them all.\n\n4. TradeBlotter component. Columns: I'll do Select, Identity, Product, Side, Executed, Current face, Price, Gross principal, Status. Security ID? \"Show useful identity, side, execution, current face, price, principal, and status columns\". Identity could include securityId as secondary text. Let me structure the identity cell: internal trade ID strong, then a small line with security ID and counterparty. Hmm counterparty not required; keep identity = internalTradeId + clientTradeId (when present) + securityId.\n\nFormat helpers in the blotter:\n```ts\nconst faceFormatter = new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en-US\", { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });\nconst principalFormatter = new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en-US\", { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });\nconst timestampFormatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(\"en-US\", { month: \"short\", day: \"numeric\", hour: \"2-digit\", minute: \"2-digit\", timeZone: \"UTC\" });\n```\nNote: Intl.DateTimeFormat without year may be odd; include year.\n\nCareful about hydration: the App is \"use client\" but the page is server-rendered; Next will SSR the client component. Intl formatters with fixed locale and UTC timezone render identically on server and client. Numbers formatted with \"en-US\" locale are deterministic.\n\nAlso the test renders the route and checks for specific strings — my new content must not break `role=\"status\"` presence and caption text \"Today's synthetic securitized-product trades\". Keep the caption exactly.\n\nI'll name formatters at module level to avoid re-creation.\n\n5. TradeReview: sections — identity, status, economics, exceptions, allocations (read-only), notes, audit history. Buttons: Edit draft (disabled when cancelled), Cancel (enabled only when booked; when disabled, show explanation text: \"Cancel is available only for booked trades.\" or reason based on status: if draft → \"This trade is a draft...\", simpler: plain explanation when not booked).\n\nI'll show:\n```tsx\nconst canEdit = trade.status !== \"cancelled\";\nconst canCancel = trade.status === \"booked\";\n```\nReview empty state message keep.\n\nAudit events formatted with timestamp via Intl formatter with UTC.\n\nExceptions: list of codes/messages with severity class.\n\n6. CSS. Let me design a full visual system. Existing stub classes used by other components:\n- `.tc-panel`, `.tc-panel-heading`, `.tc-eyebrow`, `.tc-field`, `.tc-ticket-actions`, `.tc-book-reason` (TradeTicket)\n- `.tc-insights`, `.tc-metric-grid` (DeskInsights)\n- `.tc-shell`, `.tc-hero`, `.tc-synthetic-notice`, `.tc-workspace`, `.tc-validation` (app)\n- blotter: `.tc-filter-bar`, `.tc-table-region`, `.tc-table`, `.tc-blotter`\n- review: `.tc-review`, `.tc-review-body`, `.tc-empty`\n\nNew classes I add: `.tc-status-draft` etc., `.tc-error`, `.tc-warning` etc.\n\nDistinct from the dashboard: the dashboard route — let me quickly check app/globals.css colors to keep distinct. Let me look at it.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_03128d9500013o5RqkUc1MgUoH","sessionID":"ses_fceda74b8ffec0f01p0fDyvTkH","messageID":"msg_03128429c0010oE4Oa2PNIfeL7"}}
